index_expr:
idx)), H.strip_parens(iname), iname), ")"])) # THE WHOLE DEF. Python takes `x, buf, idx` and reads `x` for nothing at all -- # it is in the signature so the `base_rewrite` arm can pass `**kwargs` -- and it # reads `buf` for its ADDRESS SPACE, its NAME and its ELEMENT COUNT, all three of # which the port takes as parameters. What is left of `buf` is nothing, and what # is left of the signature is the INDEX node alone -- which is why the third # parameter is `idx` and not `bidx`: the name `bidx` claimed to be the buffer # index and the buffer is not in this def at all. def render_index(+ar: O.Arena, +dev: U32, idx: U32, baddr: S.Addr, bname: String, iname: String, bnumel: U32, lane: Bool) -> String:   render_index.alu2(is_alu_addr(baddr), ar, dev, bname, iname, idx, bnumel, lane) # =========================================================================== # `render_buffer` -- cstyle.py:175-178, the `Ops.BUFFER` arm of `base_rewrite`. # #     prefix = f"{self.smem_align}{self.smem_prefix}" if x.addrspace == AddrSpace.LOCAL else "" #     suffix = f"[{x.max_numel()}]" #     return f"{prefix}{self._render_dtype(x.dtype)} {self[x]}{suffix};" # # FOUR THINGS, and the first produces the row that LOOKS wrong: #   * the prefix is `smem_align` FOLLOWED BY `smem_prefix`, and HIP's #     `smem_prefix` has no trailing space, so the two concatenate into #     `__attribute__((shared, aligned(16)))float` with NO space before the type. #     Measured, and a gate row precisely because a reader would "fix" it. #   * `_render_dtype(x.dtype)` is the DEFAULT ARGUMENT SHAPE -- `sz=1`, #     `addrspace=ALU` -- so a LOCAL buffer's type carries NO `*` even though a #     LOCAL POINTER does. The address space is consumed by the PREFIX here, not #     by the type. That is why the type argument is `S.Aalu{}` and not `a`. #   * `x.max_numel()` is a BUFFER's element count, which is `ParamArg.size`: a #     concrete int, so wall (b) does not apply here. #   * the trailing `;` lives in `render_buffer` and NOT in the `Ops.BUFFER` rule, #     because the rule's string is also the DECLARATION `_render` emits. # =========================================================================== def rb_prefix.of(+dev: U32, +a: S.Addr) -> String:   match a:     case S.ALocal{}: String.concat([smem_align.of(dev), smem_prefix.of(dev)])     case _: "" def rb_prefix(+dev: U32, +a: S.Addr) -> String: rb_prefix.of(dev, a) def render_buffer(+dev: U32, +d: S.Dt, numel: U32, +a: S.Addr, name: String) -> String:   String.concat([rb_prefix(dev, a), rd_base_name(dev, d), " ", name, "[", U32.show(numel), "];"]) # =========================================================================== # `code_for_op` -- cstyle.py:142-150, and the per-device overrides at :288-291, # :376, :432-438 and :532-533. `dict[Ops, Callable]`, so the ARM is a match on the # op and the DEVICE is the tag -- there is no closure to store. # # TWO SHAPES IN THE PYTHON AND BOTH MATTER: #   * UNARY (`x, dtype`) and BINARY (`a, b, dtype`) and TERNARY (`a, b, c, #     dtype`). `Ops.WHERE` is the only ternary, and it is the only arm whose #     arity differs, so a reader that threaded one argument list would emit #     `(a?b)` for WHERE. The `xs` parameter is the whole src list and the arms #     pick from it, so the arity is visible in the arm. #   * the `dtype` argument is READ by exactly six ops on CUDA (`h`/`htrunc`/ #     `hsin`/`hlog2`/`hexp2`/`hsqrt`/`hrcp` for half and bfloat16) and by Clang's #     `SQRT`/`TRUNC`/`FDIV` (the `f64` variants). Everywhere else it is ignored, #     so it is a parameter of the def rather than a per-arm read. # # THE DEVICE SPLIT IS MEASURED AND IT IS SMALL: Clang DROPS `EXP2`, `SIN`, `LOG2` # and `RECIPROCAL` entirely (they become libcalls the compiler lowers, cstyle.py: # :288) and adds `FDIV`; CUDA and HIP keep all twenty-one and override six; Metal # overrides one (`SIN` -> `precise::sin`); OpenCL and QCOM change nothing. A # dropped op is a `KeyError` in Python, so the dropped arm is a gate row. # =========================================================================== def cfo_unary(nm: String, +x: String) -> String: String.concat([nm, "(", x, ")"]) # `f"(1/{x})"` and `f"-{x}"` are NEITHER of them the unary `f"{nm}({x})"` shape, # so they are their own defs rather than a "prefix" helper with an empty name. # `cfo_prefixed("", x)` would be `f"-{x}"` by accident and `cfo_prefixed("1/", x)` # would be `f"-1/({x})"` -- the unary template has the parens INSIDE, so neither # spelling of a prefix template reaches these two. MEASURED by the oracle: # RECIPROCAL is `(1/X)` and NEG is `-X`. def cfo_recip(+x: String) -> String: String.concat(["(1/", x, ")"]) def cfo_neg(+x: String) -> String: String.concat(["-", x]) def cfo_bin(+a: String, sym: String, b: String) -> String: String.concat(["(", a, sym, b, ")"]) def cfo_tern(+a: String, b: String, c: String) -> String: String.concat(["(", a, "?", b, ":", c, ")"]) # `xs` is the src-name list, `xs0`/`xs1`/`xs2` its three positional reads. `nd` is # the number of srcs, which is the arity test: WHERE has three and everything # else has two or one, and `head`/`nth` on an empty list is the BOTTOM of the # list rather than a crash -- so an op reached with the wrong arity renders a # visibly wrong string instead of a wrong type. def xs_at(xs: List<&2, String>, n: Nat) -> String:   Maybe.default(&2, String, List.get(&2, String, xs, n), "?") def cfo_xs1(xs: List<&2, String>) -> String: xs_at(xs, 0n) def cfo_xs2(xs: List<&2, String>) -> String: xs_at(xs, 1n) def cfo_xs3(xs: List<&2, String>) -> String: xs_at(xs, 2n) # THE BASE TABLE. `Ops.WHERE` is the ternary and it is matched FIRST because the # op match is a single `match` and Python's dict has no arity to distinguish it. # THE BASE TABLE HAS NO `Ops.FDIV` ARM AND THAT IS CORRECT, NOT AN OMISSION: # cstyle.py:142-150 is a dict literal of TWENTY-ONE keys and `FDIV` is not one of # them -- Clang ADDS it (cstyle.py:291) and no other device has it. A reader that # gave the base an `FDIV` arm would answer `(X/Y)` where CPython raises # `KeyError`, and the `_` arm answers `""` here. MEASURED BY THE GATE: with an # `FDIV` arm in the base, the mutation "delete Clang's explicit FDIV arm" moved NO # ROW, because Clang then fell through to a base arm that should not have been # there. Removing it makes the Clang arm load-bearing, which is what it is. def code_for_base.of(op: O.Op, +xs: List<&2, String>) -> String:   match op:     case O.OpsSQRT{}: cfo_unary("sqrt", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsRECIPROCAL{}: cfo_recip(cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsNEG{}: cfo_neg(cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsEXP2{}: cfo_unary("exp2", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsLOG2{}: cfo_unary("log2", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsSIN{}: cfo_unary("sin", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsTRUNC{}: cfo_unary("trunc", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsAND{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "&", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsXOR{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "^", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsOR{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "|", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsADD{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "+", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsSUB{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "-", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsMUL{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "*", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsCMOD{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "%", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsCDIV{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "/", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsCMPNE{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "!=", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsSHR{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), ">>", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsSHL{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "<<", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsCMPLT{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "<", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsWHERE{}: cfo_tern(cfo_xs1(xs), cfo_xs2(xs), cfo_xs3(xs))     case O.OpsCMPEQ{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "==", cfo_xs2(xs))     case _: "" # =========================================================================== # THE PER-DEVICE ALU OVERRIDES. Six ops on CUDA, five on HIP, one on Metal, two # on Clang, and the FIVE THAT ARE DROPPED. `is_half` is the `dtype in (half, # bfloat16)` test, and it is a `Bool` PARAMETER rather than a dtype so the # override tables do not each re-derive it. # =========================================================================== def is_half(+d: S.Dt) -> Bool:   Bool.or(O.eq_dt(d, S.half()), O.eq_dt(d, S.bfloat16())) def is_f64(+d: S.Dt) -> Bool: O.eq_dt(d, S.double()) # THERE IS NO `is_f32`, and the absence is load-bearing rather than an omission: # Clang's suffix rule is `f` UNLESS f64 (cstyle.py:288-289) and HIP's `_ocml` map # is `{half:16, double:64}.get(dtype, 32)` with 32 as the DEFAULT -- so `float` # reaches both by falling through, and a third predicate would be a fourth way to # spell "not one of those two". # CLANG: `SQRT` and `TRUNC` pick the `f64` spelling by dtype, `FDIV` is ADDED, # and `EXP2`/`SIN`/`LOG2`/`RECIPROCAL` are DELETED (cstyle.py:288-291). The # comprehension is `{k:v for k,v in base.items() if k not in [EXP2, SIN, LOG2, # TRUNC, RECIPROCAL]}` and then TRUNC and FDIV and SQRT are re-set, so TRUNC # SURVIVES and the other three do not. The deletion is the load-bearing half and # `""` is its answer -- a `KeyError` in Python, an empty string here, and the # difference is a visible gate row rather than a crash. # # THE SUFFIX IS `f` UNLESS THE DTYPE IS f64, and there is no separate f32 case: # Clang emits `__builtin_sqrtf(X)` for float AND for half and # `__builtin_sqrt(X)` for double. MEASURED, all three. def ocml_or(+base: String, suf: String, f64: Bool) -> String:   Bool.pick(String, f64, base, String.concat([base, suf])) def code_for_clang.of(op: O.Op, +xs: List<&2, String>, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   match op:     case O.OpsSQRT{}: cfo_unary(ocml_or("__builtin_sqrt", "f", is_f64(d)), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsTRUNC{}: cfo_unary(ocml_or("__builtin_trunc", "f", is_f64(d)), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsFDIV{}: cfo_bin(cfo_xs1(xs), "/", cfo_xs2(xs))     case O.OpsEXP2{}: ""     case O.OpsSIN{}: ""     case O.OpsLOG2{}: ""     case O.OpsRECIPROCAL{}: ""     case _: code_for_base.of(op, xs) # METAL: `SIN` is the ONLY override and it is `precise::sin` for every dtype # (cstyle.py:376). def code_for_metal.of(op: O.Op, +xs: List<&2, String>, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   match op:     case O.OpsSIN{}: cfo_unary("precise::sin", cfo_xs1(xs))     case _: code_for_base.of(op, xs) # CUDA: `htrunc`/`hsin`/`hlog2`/`hexp2`/`hsqrt`/`hrcp` for half and bfloat16, and # the PLAIN form otherwise (cstyle.py:432-438). Six ops, one `Bool`. def cuda_pick(half: Bool, hnm: String, nm: String, +x: String) -> String:   Bool.pick(String, half, cfo_unary(hnm, x), cfo_unary(nm, x)) # HIP: `_ocml(op)` is `f"__ocml_{op}_f{ {half:16, double:64}.get(dtype, 32)}({x})"` # (cstyle.py:493) -- the WIDTH, not a dtype name, and 32 is the default for # everything else including f32. So the map is a two-entry lookup with a 32 # fallback and the `f` is always there. def ocml_bits(+d: S.Dt) -> U32:   Bool.pick(U32, O.eq_dt(d, S.half()), 16, Bool.pick(U32, is_f64(d), 64, 32)) def ocml_name(op: String, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   String.concat(["__ocml_", op, "_f", U32.show(ocml_bits(d))]) def code_for_hip.of(op: O.Op, +xs: List<&2, String>, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   match op:     case O.OpsTRUNC{}: cfo_unary(ocml_name("trunc", d), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsSIN{}: cfo_unary(ocml_name("sin", d), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsLOG2{}: cfo_unary(ocml_name("log2", d), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsEXP2{}: cfo_unary(ocml_name("exp2", d), cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsSQRT{}: cfo_unary(ocml_name("sqrt", d), cfo_xs1(xs))     case _: code_for_base.of(op, xs) def code_for_cuda.of(op: O.Op, +xs: List<&2, String>, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   match op:     case O.OpsTRUNC{}: cuda_pick(is_half(d), "htrunc", "trunc", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsSIN{}: cuda_pick(is_half(d), "hsin", "sin", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsLOG2{}: cuda_pick(is_half(d), "hlog2", "log2", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsEXP2{}: cuda_pick(is_half(d), "hexp2", "exp2", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsSQRT{}: cuda_pick(is_half(d), "hsqrt", "sqrt", cfo_xs1(xs))     case O.OpsRECIPROCAL{}: Bool.pick(String, is_half(d), cfo_unary("hrcp", cfo_xs1(xs)), cfo_recip(cfo_xs1(xs)))     case _: code_for_base.of(op, xs) # THE DISPATCH. Five devices and the base, and OpenCL and QCOM are the BASE -- # measured: neither overrides a single ALU op, and the gate's `cfo` rows are # what says so rather than a comment. def code_for_op.of(+dev: U32, op: O.Op, xs: List<&2, String>, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   match dev:     case 1: code_for_clang.of(op, xs, d)     case 3: code_for_metal.of(op, xs, d)     case 4: code_for_cuda.of(op, xs, d)     case 5: code_for_hip.of(op, xs, d)     case _: code_for_base.of(op, xs) # =========================================================================== # `code_for_workitem` -- cstyle.py:134, :330, :370, :431, :531. Five devices # spell the workitem id and the BASE has an EMPTY dict, so a SPECIAL on the base # CStyleLanguage is a `KeyError` in Python. `""` is the port's marker and it is # NOT reachable for a real kernel: every GPU renderer defines both entries. # # THE THREE SPELLINGS, and the third is the interesting one: Metal and CUDA # INDEX A MEMBER BY ASCII -- `chr(120 + int(x))` on a STRING argument, so `x` is # the workitem index as a decimal string and `int(x)` is 0, 1 or 2. HIP and # OpenCL pass the string STRAIGHT INTO the builtin, so `get_group_id(0)` is # literally that. The port keeps the `U32` and formats it, which is the same # answer for 0..2 and is stated because `int("07")` in Python is 7 and # `U32.show(7)` is `"7"`. # =========================================================================== def witem_xyz(n: U32) -> String: String.from_list([Char.from_u32(U32.add(120, n))]) def code_for_workitem.g(+dev: U32, +k: String, n: U32) -> String:   match dev:     case 2: String.concat([Bool.pick(String, String.eq(k, "g"), "get_group_id(", "get_local_id("), U32.show(n), ")"])     case 3: String.concat([Bool.pick(String, String.eq(k, "g"), "gid.", "lid."), witem_xyz(n)])     case 4: String.concat([Bool.pick(String, String.eq(k, "g"), "blockIdx.", "threadIdx."), witem_xyz(n)])     case 5: String.concat([Bool.pick(String, String.eq(k, "g"), "__ockl_get_group_id(", "__ockl_get_local_id("), U32.show(n), ")"])     case _: "" # =========================================================================== # `_wmma_name` -- cstyle.py:115-117, and the one place a NAME is built from a # dtype and sanitised. # #     return f"WMMA_{'_'.join(map(str, u.arg[0]))}_{u.arg[1].name}_{u.dtype.name}".replace(" ", "_") # # THE SANITISE IS THE WHOLE POINT and it is NOT conditional: `int8.name` is # `"signed char"`, so without the replace the name is # `WMMA_16_16_16_signed char_float`, which is not a C identifier. With it, the # name is `WMMA_16_16_16_signed_char_float`. The same replace machinery as # `_render_dtype` serves both, and the gate's `wmma_*` rows pin the space case # specifically -- an implementation that reused the C NAME spelling but dropped # the replace would produce a name no compiler accepts. # # `u.dtype` is the OUTPUT dtype and `u.arg[1].name` the INPUT, and they are # spelled from different places, so a reader that used one for both would be right # on the three fixtures where they coincide and wrong on the rest. # =========================================================================== def wmma_dims_go(ds: List<&2, U32>, acc: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>:   match ds:     case Nil{}: acc     case h <> t: wmma_dims_go(t, List.append(&2, String, acc, [U32.show(h)])) def wmma_dims(ds: List<&2, U32>) -> String: String.join(wmma_dims_go(ds, Nil{}), "_") # `'_'.join(map(str, u.arg[0]))` -- the arg is `AWmma{dims, dt, threads, tc}`. def wmma_dims.of(+a: O.Arg) -> String:   match a:     case O.AWmma{dims, dt, threads, tc}: wmma_dims(dims)     case _: "" # `u.arg[1].name` -- the INPUT dtype. def wmma_in.of(+a: O.Arg) -> String:   match a:     case O.AWmma{dims, dt, threads, tc}: dt_name(dt)     case _: "" # `f"WMMA_{dims}_{in}_{out}".replace(" ", "_")` -- the replace is UNCONDITIONAL, # unlike `_render_dtype`'s. def wmma_name_of(dims: String, din: String, dout: String) -> String:   under(String.concat(["WMMA_", dims, "_", din, "_", dout])) def wmma_name(+a: O.Arg, dout: S.Dt) -> String:   wmma_name_of(wmma_dims.of(a), wmma_in.of(a), dt_name(dout)) # =========================================================================== # `uops_to_dtypes` -- cstyle.py:112-113. # #     return dedup((u.dtype, u.max_numel()) for u in uops if u.addrspace in (AddrSpace.ALU, None) and u.dtype != dtypes.void and u._shape is not None) # # THREE FILTERS AND THEY ARE NOT INDEPENDENT. `addrspace in (ALU, None)` is the # one that keeps a REGISTER value out (a `val0` on a GPU is ALU, a `gid` is # REG), `dtype != void` drops a SINK, and `_shape is not None` drops a node the # fold could not shape. The port's `addr` is `S.Addr` and Python's `None` is not # one of its four values -- it is what `fold.addr` answers for a node whose # sources disagree -- so the port's filter is `ALU` alone and the `None` arm is # the `TODO(p3)` at the foot. # # `dedup` RETAINS LIST ORDER (helpers.py:23, `list(dict.fromkeys(x))`) and the # order is the gate, because the RESULT FEEDS `ClangRenderer._render_defines` # and the `typedef`s come out in it. # =========================================================================== # `uops_to_dtypes` ITSELF IS NOT HERE, and the two filters it applies are not # separate defs either: both are already one Bool each in the `Uses` record # above (`is_alu_addr` is the ALU filter and `is_void` is `dtype != dtypes.void`), # so a def per filter would be a second spelling of a field. #   TODO(p3) cstyle.py:112-113  `uops_to_dtypes`. Needs the fold (wall (a)); its #   result ORDER feeds `ClangRenderer._render_defines`, so it is not a set. # =========================================================================== # `render_kernel` -- cstyle.py:154-166. THE function that assembles a whole # kernel, and the only place in this file that reads nine options at once. # #     buftypes = [(name, ("volatile_ " if u.arg.volatile_ else "")+ #                    (self.var_prefix if u.addrspace == AddrSpace.ALU else "")+ #                    self._render_dtype(u.dtype, sz=1, addrspace=u.addrspace, mutable=mutable, shape=u._shape)+ #                    (self.var_suffix if u.addrspace == AddrSpace.ALU else self.buffer_suffix)) #                for name,(u,mutable) in bufs] #     local_dims = [u.src[0] for u in uops if u.op is Ops.SPECIAL and u.arg[0] == "l"] #     launch_bounds = prod([d.vmax for d in local_dims]) #     prg = ''.join([f"{self.kernel_typedef.format(launch_bounds=launch_bounds)} {function_name}(",] + #               [', '.join([f'{t} {name}' for name,t in buftypes] + self.extra_args)] + #               [") {
" + tmp] + ['
'.join(kernel), "
}"]) #     return prg if prefix is None else "
".join(prefix)+f"
{prg}" # # FIVE THINGS, AND THE THIRD IS THE ONE THAT SAYS A DROPPED LITERAL IS A DROPPED # LITERAL RATHER THAN A COMPILE ERROR: #   * `launch_bounds = prod([d.vmax for d in local_dims])` and `prod(())` is 1 -- #     so a kernel with NO local SPECIAL gets `__launch_bounds__(1)`, not 0. The #     gate's `kern nolocal` row is exactly that case, and a reader that started #     the accumulator at 0 would emit `(0)`. #   * `prefix is None` is the WHOLE BRANCH, and `[]` is not `None`: an empty #     prefix list must NOT gain a leading newline. Metal's prefix is #     non-empty and CUDA's is four lines, so the two cases both occur. #   * `extra_args` is Metal's THREE lines (cstyle.py:372) and it is appended to #     the SAME `', '.join` as the buffer types, so Metal's kernel signature is #     `kernel void E_4(device float* data0_4, constant args_t& args #     [[buffer(0)]], uint3 gid [[...]], uint3 lid [[...]])`. The port takes #     `extra_args` as a `List<&2, String>` and joins it into the same list. #   * `launch_bounds` comes from `d.vmax` -- a SYMBOLIC maximum, and the #     `TODO(p3) ops.py:1886` wall again. It is a `U32` PARAMETER here, and the #     SPECIAL's `vmax` on a linearized kernel is its CONST end. #   * `kernel_typedef.format(launch_bounds=..)` is a `str.format`, and there is no #     `format` in base.bend, so the `{launch_bounds}` FIELD is substituted by a #     split on the literal and a join -- `render.bend`'s shape for a Python #     f-string the port cannot evaluate. # =========================================================================== # `local_dims = [u.src[0] for u in uops if u.op is Ops.SPECIAL and u.arg[0]=="l"]` # and then `prod([d.vmax ...])`: `launch_bounds` is a `U32` PARAMETER above, and # this is where it would be computed. NEITHER HALF IS PORTED and the reason is # the same on both sides: the fold (wall (a)) owns the uop list, and `d.vmax` is # the SYMBOLIC maximum that is `TODO(p3) ops.py:1886`. The SPECIAL filter itself # is one string test on the arg -- `arg[0]` of `("l", 0, "lidx0", "l")` is `"l"` # -- so it is a `head_char` over an `AStr` once the arena is walkable, and the # gate's `kern lb=1` rows are the no-local case it has to agree with. #   TODO(p3) cstyle.py:157, :160  `local_dims` and `launch_bounds`. # `case p <> t` on a `String` gives the first CHARACTER (measured, render.bend # rule 12) and that is exactly `arg[0]`. # THE SIGNATURE. `f'{t} {name}'` for each buffer, then `extra_args`, joined with # ", ". `args` is the ALREADY-FORMATTED `t name` list, so `render_kernel` does the # formatting and this def only joins -- which is what makes the two halves # separately gateable. # # `extra_args` -- cstyle.py:372, and ONLY Metal sets it. Three lines appended to # the SAME `", ".join` as the buffer types, which is why a Metal kernel signature # carries `constant args_t& args [[buffer(0)]]` between the buffers and the two # `uint3` position attributes. def extra_args.dev(dev: U32) -> List<&2, String>:   match dev:     case 3: ["constant args_t& args [[buffer(0)]]", "uint3 gid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]]", "uint3 lid [[thread_position_in_threadgroup]]"]     case _: Nil{} # `f'{t} {name}'` for one buffer -- cstyle.py:158-160, the `buftypes` element. # `volatile_` rides in FRONT when the ParamArg says so and `var_prefix` / # `var_suffix` REPLACE `buffer_suffix` for an ALU buffer, which is a different # condition and not an addition. # # THE LITERAL IS `"volatile "` AND NOT `"volatile_ "` -- the FIELD is spelled # `volatile_` because `volatile` is a RESERVED WORD (bend2-constraints rule 25), # but the EMITTED C is upstream's `volatile` with a space, and the escape is on # the Bend name only. MEASURED: the `buf3 volatile` row, which is the only row # with a volatile buffer; a reader that echoed the field name emits an identifier # no C compiler accepts. def bt_prefix.of(volatile_: Bool, varp: String, +is_alu: Bool) -> String:   String.concat([Bool.pick(String, volatile_, "volatile ", ""), Bool.pick(String, is_alu, varp, "")]) def bt_suffix.of(+is_alu: Bool, vars: String, bufs: String) -> String:   Bool.pick(String, is_alu, vars, bufs) # `u.addrspace == AddrSpace.ALU` -- AND IT IS `is_alu_addr` AGAIN, not a second # spelling. Two defs matching `S.Aalu{}` would be two places for the ALU test to # drift, and `render_index` already needs it. def buftype(+dev: U32, +b: BArg) -> String:   String.concat([bt_prefix.of(BArg.volatile_(b), var_prefix.of(dev), is_alu_addr(BArg.addr(b))),     render_dtype(dev, BArg.dtype(b), 1, BArg.addr(b), BArg.mutable(b), False{}, BArg.image(b)),     bt_suffix.of(is_alu_addr(BArg.addr(b)), var_suffix.of(dev), buffer_suffix.of(dev)), " ", BArg.name(b)]) def buftypes.go(+dev: U32, bs: List<&2, BArg>, acc: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>:   match bs:     case Nil{}: acc     case h <> t: buftypes.go(dev, t, List.append(&2, String, acc, [buftype(dev, h)])) def buftypes(+dev: U32, +bs: List<&2, BArg>) -> List<&2, String>: buftypes.go(dev, bs, Nil{}) # =========================================================================== # THE SIX `render_kernel` OVERRIDES. cstyle.py:310 (Clang), :348 (OpenCL), :390 # (Metal), :454 (CUDA), :555 (HIP); the base has none. Every one of them builds a # `prefix` LIST and then calls `super().render_kernel` -- except Clang, which # builds a `defines` string and a trailing newline instead. Four things are # load-bearing about that and all four are gate rows, because the failure mode is # a kernel that COMPILES: # #   * `prefix=[]` IS NOT `prefix=None`. cstyle.py:166 is `prg if prefix is None #     else "
".join(prefix)+f"
{prg}"`, so an empty list puts a LEADING NEWLINE #     in the output. CUDA and HIP hit this on EVERY kernel: their overrides #     ASSIGN a prefix, and the assignment is `prefix = [...]` or `prefix, ockl = #     [], []` -- never `None`. MEASURED, `kern2 HIP` begins with a newline and #     `kern2 OPENCL` does not. #   * THREE OF THE SIX DISCARD THE CALLER'S PREFIX. CUDA, HIP and Metal all #     assign `prefix` before calling super, so a `#pragma` the caller passed in #     is dropped. MEASURED, `render_kernel(..., prefix=[two lines])` on CUDA and #     HIP returns BYTE-IDENTICAL output to `prefix=None`. #   * OPENCL IS THE ONE THAT PREPENDS, and it prepends onto the CALLER's list, #     not onto its own: `["#pragma ..."] + (prefix or [])` (cstyle.py:349). #   * CLANG IS NOT A PREFIX AT ALL. cstyle.py:310-312 is #     `defines + "
" + body + "
" + entry`, so Clang is the ONLY renderer whose #     output gains BOTH a leading and a trailing newline, and `_render_entry` is #     `""` on every path (cstyle.py:308) so the trailing one is unconditional. # # THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS FILE GOT ALL FOUR WRONG for Clang, HIP and Metal and # every gate row passed anyway, because those rows were the only ones whose text # spanned more than one line and a row-keyed diff cannot see a row it does not # parse. `esc_row` below is the fix and the reason a row is one line is written # down at its definition. # =========================================================================== # `prefix += xs` (cstyle.py:459-463, :567-579). Named because four of the five # overrides are `prefix = a` then `prefix += b`, and a reader that wrote `a + b` # as a STRING concatenation would join with the wrong separator. def add(a: List<&2, String>, b: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>: List.append(&2, String, a, b) # `prefix.append(x) if <test>` -- the shape of nine of the eleven `if`s in the # two vendor overrides. `inc_if` is the whole conditional-append idiom. def inc_if(on: Bool, s: String) -> List<&2, String>: Bool.pick(List<&2, String>, on, [s], Nil{}) # CUDA's four unconditional lines (cstyle.py:456-457). `tg_bitcast` is one line # in the source and one line in the output, which is why it is a single string # here rather than a def: nothing in it varies with the device or the kernel. def cuda_static() -> List<&2, String>:   ["typedef unsigned int uint;", "#define INFINITY (__int_as_float(0x7f800000))",    "#define NAN (__int_as_float(0x7fffffff))",    "template <class T, class F> __device__ __forceinline__ T tg_bitcast(F v) { union U { F f; T t; }; U u; u.f = v; return u.t; }"] # HIP's `ockl` -- cstyle.py:563. Three externs in declaration order, and the # order is the order `code_for_workitem` reads them back (`__ockl_get_local_id` # is the `l` form and `__ockl_get_group_id` the `g` one). def ockl_extern(nm: String) -> String:   String.concat(["extern "C" __attribute__((device, const)) size_t __ockl_get_", nm, "(unsigned int);"]) def hip_ockl() -> List<&2, String>: [ockl_extern("local_id"), ockl_extern("group_id"), ockl_extern("local_size")] # HIP's `ocml` extern (cstyle.py:564-566, :578). `ocml_ops[op]` is a PAIR -- # (`"sqrt"`, `"const"`) -- and the second element's EMPTY case is the one that # matters, because SIN and TRUNC are the only two rows that produce # `__attribute__((device))` with no comma in it. The width is `ocml_bits`, the # same def `code_for_op` reads, so the f16/f32/f64 spelling is computed once. # # `ocml_ops`' first element is the C NAME (`sqrt`), not `Ops.SQRT.name` (`SQRT`), # and it is its OWN def rather than a table lookup inside `ocml_extern` so that # `code_for_op`'s five HIP arms and the extern cannot disagree: `SQRT` -> `sqrt` # and `""` -> `""` is the identity that makes both work. It is declared ABOVE # `ocml_extern` because a def may only call defs above it, which is the whole # mechanical cost of not having first-class functions. def op_of_cname(op: String) -> String:   match op:     case "SQRT": "sqrt"     case "TRUNC": "trunc"     case "SIN": "sin"     case "LOG2": "log2"     case "EXP2": "exp2"     case _: "" def ocml_atr.of(op: String) -> String:   match op:     case "SQRT": "const"     case "EXP2": "pure"     case "LOG2": "pure"     case _: "" # `f'extern "C" __attribute__((device{f", {atr}" if atr else ""})) {dto} {meth}({dti});'` # -- cstyle.py:578. THE COMMA IS PART OF THE ATTRIBUTE AND NOT OF THE SPELLING, # so the `""` case is `__attribute__((device))` with NO trailing space: a reader # that writes `"(device, "` unconditionally emits `__attribute__((device, ))` on # SIN and TRUNC, which HIP accepts and no other compiler does, and the `hipocml` # row is the only thing that can see it. # # `{dto}` AND `{dti}` ARE `self.render_dtype(dt)`, which is `_render_dtype(dt, 1, # AddrSpace.REG)` -- the BASE `type_map` lookup, so `half`/`float`/`double` and # NOT the rust `DType.name`. MEASURED against the live tree: with `dt_name` here # the `hipocml` row and the `kern2 HIP ockl` row printed `f16`/`f32` and CPython # printed `half`/`float`, and both `py=` literals had been transcribed from the PIN # so the two agreed and the diff was empty. `rd_base_name(dev_base(), d)` is the # same lookup the base device answers. def ocml_extern(+op: String, +d: S.Dt) -> String:   String.concat(["extern "C" __attribute__((device", Bool.pick(String, String.eq(ocml_atr.of(op), ""), "", ", "), ocml_atr.of(op), ")) ", rd_base_name(dev_base(), d), " ",     ocml_name(op_of_cname(op), d), "(", rd_base_name(dev_base(), d), ");"]) # THE ORDER OF THE PREFIX IS DATA. CUDA emits five clauses and HIP eight, in the # order `prefix +=` fixes, and the emitted order IS the call order -- "fp8 before # fp16 before bf16" and "size_t before hip_bfloat16 before half" are facts about # the generated header and not about formatting. A fold over an integer index is # the shortest expression of that: the order becomes a RANGE, so reordering the # clauses means changing which number each clause sits at, which is visible. def prefix_clauses.of(+dev: U32) -> U32:   match dev:     case 4: 5     case 5: 8     case _: 0 def prefix_clause.of(+dev: U32, +u: Uses, +vecs: List<&2, String>, +ockl: List<&2, String>, +ocml: List<&2, String>, cdna4: Bool, k: U32) -> List<&2, String>:   match dev:     case 4:       match k:         case 0: cuda_static()         case 1: inc_if(Uses.fp8(u), "#include <cuda_fp8.h>")         case 2: inc_if(Uses.half(u), "#include <cuda_fp16.h>")         case 3: inc_if(Uses.bf16(u), "#include <cuda_bf16.h>")         case _: vecs     case 5:       match k:         case 0: inc_if(Uses.nonfinite(u), "#define INFINITY (__builtin_inff())")         case 1: inc_if(Uses.nonfinite(u), "#define NAN (__builtin_nanf(""))")         case 2: inc_if(Uses.special(u), "typedef long unsigned int size_t;")         case 3: inc_if(Uses.bf16(u), String.concat(["typedef ", Bool.pick(String, cdna4, "__bf16", "unsigned short"), " hip_bfloat16;"]))         case 4: inc_if(Uses.half(u), "#define half _Float16")         case 5: add(inc_if(Uses.fp8(u), "typedef unsigned char hip_bf8;"), inc_if(Uses.fp8(u), "typedef unsigned char hip_fp8;"))         case 6: add(Bool.pick(List<&2, String>, Uses.special(u), ockl, Nil{}), ocml)         case _: vecs     case _: Nil{} # ONE SELF-RECURSIVE DEF WITH A COUNTDOWN, AND THE PREVIOUS TWO-DEF SHAPE IS # WHY. The obvious `go`/`at` pair -- `go` computes `same = k == count` and calls # `at`, `at` matches on it and calls `go` -- is MUTUAL RECURSION, which Bend # refuses, and the error only appears once the ordering is fixed ("expected : a # filled definition"). Introducing the `same` PARAMETER was necessary (a `match` # may not scrutinise `U32.is_eq(k, ...)`) and it is not sufficient: convention 9 # says the self-call must live in the def that owns the `match`, so the match and # the call collapse into one def and the countdown IS the match. # # THE COUNTDOWN IS THE REMAINING CLAUSE COUNT, NOT `k`, and that is the whole # shape: `k` only GROWS and the decrease checker wants the first argument to be a # strict subterm, so `rem` is first, is a `Nat`, and hands down `m`. `rem == 0` is # the base and the port's other devices' `_` arm -- a base with no prefix is an # EMPTY list, not the base's empty string. # # `k` IS `+` FOR THE OBVIOUS REASON AND IT IS NOT AFFECTED BY THE `rem` DEGREE # CHECK: the `+` is on the SEVENTH argument and the decrease is the FIRST one. def dev_prefix.go(rem: Nat, +dev: U32, +u: Uses, +vecs: List<&2, String>, +ockl: List<&2, String>,   +ocml: List<&2, String>, +cdna4: Bool, +k: U32, acc: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>:   match rem:     case 0n: acc     case 1n+m: dev_prefix.go(m, dev, u, vecs, ockl, ocml, cdna4, U32.add(k, 1),       add(acc, prefix_clause.of(dev, u, vecs, ockl, ocml, cdna4, k))) def dev_prefix(+dev: U32, +u: Uses, +vecs: List<&2, String>, +ockl: List<&2, String>, +ocml: List<&2, String>, cdna4: Bool) -> List<&2, String>:   dev_prefix.go(U32.to_nat(prefix_clauses.of(dev)), dev, u, vecs, ockl, ocml, cdna4, 0, Nil{}) # OPENCL'S ONE PREFIX -- cstyle.py:349. It PREPENDS onto the caller's list, which # is the only place in the six where the caller's lines survive alongside the # device's, and it is conditional on a half dtype being USED (an ALU uop of that # dtype, not a buffer of it -- `uops_to_dtypes` filters to `AddrSpace.ALU`). def opencl_prefix(+u: Uses) -> List<&2, String>: inc_if(Uses.half(u), "#pragma OPENCL EXTENSION cl_khr_fp16 : enable") # METAL'S `args_t` INDIRECTION -- cstyle.py:400-403. Metal passes `bufs=[]` to # `super()` and prepends ONE line that unpacks the struct, so a Metal kernel # carries the buffer NAMES in its body and not in its signature, and the # signature has the three `extra_args` alone. # # ONE WALK AND ONE ELEMENT BECAUSE THE ELEMENT IS READ TWICE WITH ONE DIFFERENCE. # Python builds `args` once (cstyle.py:401) and reads it twice: # #     "struct args_t { " + " ".join(f"{t} {n};" for n, t in args) + " };" #     ["  " + " ".join(f"{t} {n} = args.{n};" for n, t in args)] + kernel # # The difference is a MIDDLE, not a suffix: the body spelling repeats the buffer # NAME (`data0_4 = args.data0_4`) and so has TWO names where the struct has ONE, # and the `;` is inside the element in BOTH readings. So `mid` is `""` for the # struct and `" = args."` for the body, and the SECOND name rides `mid`'s # non-emptiness -- which is the whole test. The first version emitted the name # unconditionally and produced `struct args_t { device float* data0_4data0_4; }`, # and a version that put the `;` after the JOIN produced # `device float* data0_4 = args. device float* data1_4 = args.;`. def metal_field.of(+dev: U32, +b: BArg, +mid: String) -> String:   String.concat([render_dtype(dev, BArg.dtype(b), 1, BArg.addr(b), True{}, False{}, False{}),     " ", BArg.name(b), mid, Bool.pick(String, String.eq(mid, ""), "", BArg.name(b)), ";"]) def metal_fields.go(+dev: U32, bs: List<&2, BArg>, +mid: String, acc: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>:   match bs:     case Nil{}: acc     case h <> t: metal_fields.go(dev, t, mid, List.append(&2, String, acc, [metal_field.of(dev, h, mid)])) def metal_fields(+dev: U32, +bs: List<&2, BArg>, +mid: String) -> List<&2, String>:   metal_fields.go(dev, bs, mid, Nil{}) def metal_prefix(+dev: U32, +bs: List<&2, BArg>) -> List<&2, String>:   ["#include <metal_stdlib>", "using namespace metal;",    String.concat(["struct args_t { ", String.join(metal_fields(dev, bs, ""), " "), " };"])] # THE ARGS LINE GOES IN FRONT OF THE KERNEL. `["  " + ...] + kernel` PREPENDS, and # a version that appended it put the unpacking line after the kernel body -- a # kernel that reads its arguments after it has already used them. `add` is # `a ++ b` and `List.append` is the sanctioned spelling (brief rule 6). def metal_body(+dev: U32, +bs: List<&2, BArg>, +kernel: List<&2, String>) -> List<&2, String>:   add([String.concat(["  ", String.join(metal_fields(dev
